.TH SMARTIMAGEDIFF_PSNR 1 "2026-09-03" "smartmet-library-regression" "SmartMet Regression Tools"
.SH NAME
smartimagediff_psnr \- compare two images and print the PSNR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartimagediff_psnr
.I image1
.I image2
.RI [ diff_output ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smartimagediff_psnr
loads two images via ImageMagick (Magick++), requires that they have
identical width, height and bit depth, computes the mean\(hysquared
error between them, and prints the corresponding peak signal\(hyto\(hynoise
ratio in decibels:
.PP
.RS 4
.B PSNR:
.I value
.B dB
.RE
.PP
Identical images print
.B PSNR: inf dB
(infinite ratio); larger numbers indicate more similar images. This is
the measurement engine behind the PSNR verdict of
.BR smartpngdiff (1).
.PP
When the optional
.I diff_output
argument is given, a difference image is written to that path. It is
produced with the
.B Difference
composite operator and histogram\(hyequalized, which makes even small
pixel deltas visible \(em at the price of amplifying harmless
anti\(hyaliasing noise over the whole frame. For a difference image that
points at the actual change instead, see
.BR smartimagediff (1).
.PP
A mismatch in dimensions or bit depth, an unreadable image or a wrong
number of arguments is reported on standard error as
.BI "Error: " message
(or as a usage line) and the exit status is
.BR 1 .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I image1
First image to compare.
.TP
.I image2
Second image to compare.
.TP
.I diff_output
Optional output path for the equalized difference image.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
PSNR was computed and printed.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong number of arguments, unreadable image, or images differing in
size or depth.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compare two PNG files:
.PP
.RS 4
smartimagediff_psnr expected.png actual.png
.RE
.PP
Compare and write a difference image:
.PP
.RS 4
smartimagediff_psnr expected.png actual.png diff.png
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartpngdiff (1),
.BR smartimagediff (1),
.BR magick (1),
.BR compare (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Finnish Meteorological Institute
.PP
